On normal levels where only one troll at a time usually
appears, the most common methods are to eat the corpse,
offer the corpse at an altar, or to keep killing the
troll again and again until it no longer revives.  That
last method gives you plenty of extra experience points
and some death-drop items.

On a Quest level you could use conflict and depend on
the fact that each time a troll dies there is some
chance it will rot away before it revives.

Or consider the strategy I use with Valkyries: Go into
the Quest, manuever one giant far away from the others,
kill it, eat it.  Ignore the messages that you stopped
eating and try again until finished.  Then go back out
to the main dungeon and explore until you stop being
Satiated.  Return to the Quest and eat another giant.
Valks do this to get the strength from the giant
corpses but a Barbarian could do it just to have fewer
trolls to face.

